# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files — secrets never get committed.
# The template is the one deliberate exception: it documents every variable the
# project reads, with no values in it.
.env*
!.env.example

# storybook build output — a generated artifact, not source
storybook-static

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Audit-only legacy asset area.
#
# Copies of legacy southdademusic.com assets pulled down for visual
# provenance/consent review. They are NOT approved media and NOT deployable:
#
#   · never committed
#   · never imported by application code
#   · never referenced by a public route
#   · never copied into public/
#
# Gates I-1 (photo-release consent) and I-7 (photographer copyright) remain in
# force for every file in here. Phase 4D put five such files in public/ on
# filename evidence alone; all five were photographs of identifiable people,
# two including children. This directory exists so that inspection can happen
# WITHOUT that risk.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.audit/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MI1 local media-review derivatives.
#
# Crops and resizes generated from .audit/legacy-assets/ so the team can see
# how authentic South Dade photography changes the approved design.
#
# ⚠️ PREVIEW ONLY — NOT CLEARED FOR PRODUCTION.
#   · every derivative still sits behind I-7 (photographer copyright)
#   · people-bearing sources stay in .audit/ and are never derived from here
#   · this directory is gitignored so it cannot enter a commit or a deploy
#   · a development-only badge marks any page rendering these
# Provenance for each file: # (moved to .audit/media-review — see below)_derivatives.json
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
public/_media-review/
